mh2lm: reduce battery-source poll cadence to two seconds

The m15 hardware log establishes that PM8150B VBUS changes are correctly
observable and that SweetBattery::publish() notifies IOPM consumers via
updateStatus().  The service nevertheless arms its only timer at 30 seconds,
so an insertion/removal can leave the status-bar icon stale for almost half a
minute.  Use a single 2-second read-only cadence for the SID2 and legacy
paths.  This patch does not change source properties, charger state decoding,
or any PMIC register; it only schedules the existing observer reads sooner.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetBattery.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetBattery.cpp
index 20f2a3b..8d74e25 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetBattery.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetBattery.cpp
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
